  "caveats": [
    "Model v1 is pose-only. No paired pose+EMG training data exists yet (see MASTER_BUILD_PLAN_v3.md \u00a79 'Known gaps'). EMG stays a live display and a rep-validity pre-filter joined on timestamp_ms -- never a fused model feature -- until paired data lands.",
    "Every recording in this dataset shares a single subject_id (one actor). GroupKFold below is therefore recording-level, not subject-level. Nothing here estimates cross-patient generalization.",
    "Dataset is small (11-64 clips per exercise). RandomForest is deliberately shallow (max_depth=4) and XGBoost deliberately regularized for this reason; both still risk coincidental splits.",
    "Rep segmentation for live sessions is unbuilt (I3). This model was trained on hand-cut clips; production gets continuous video.",
    "Isometric exercises (seated_knee_extension) have no trained error model that clears the CV gate -- all positives concentrate in one recording group. Rule-based only until more recordings exist.",
    "See docs/06_ml_pipeline.md for the full E8 label-circularity audit. Two labels (mini_squat's derivative of path_deviation, and straight_leg_raise's knee_flexion_high) were found to be thresholded directly from a feature-derived signal; treat any near-1.000 score on those labels as evidence of leakage, not of quality."
